---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SERVER } from '../consts.ts';
---
<Base title="Rules — GibbSux">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">HOUSE RULES</span>
      <h2>Rules</h2>
      <p class="lead">Short list. It comes down to not ruining the game for anyone else.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-bottom:34px">
      <div class="card accent-red">
        <h3>No griefing</h3>
        <p>Don't break, burn or steal from other people's builds. Ever. This is the one
        that gets you removed immediately and without discussion.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-red">
        <h3>No cheating</h3>
        <p>X-ray, kill aura, auto-clickers, flight, reach, freecam. If it gives you an
        advantage the rest of us don't have, it isn't allowed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-red">
        <h3>No lag machines</h3>
        <p>Giant mob farms, endless dispenser clocks and chunk-loading contraptions hurt
        everyone. This server runs on a Raspberry Pi — be reasonable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-green">
        <h3>Build with space</h3>
        <p>The world is unlimited. Don't build right on top of someone unless they've
        said it's fine.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-green">
        <h3>Be decent</h3>
        <p>No slurs, no harassment, no drama. Everyone here got in because someone
        vouched for them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-green">
        <h3>Ask before big changes</h3>
        <p>Terraforming a mountain, draining an ocean, redirecting a river near others —
        just mention it first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card-flat accent-amber">
      <h3>What happens if you break them</h3>
      <p class="muted small">There's no warning system or ticket process. Griefing gets you banned
      and the damage restored from the nightly backup, which costs everyone else their progress
      since the last save. That's why the rule is absolute rather than negotiable.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:60px"><h2 style="font-size:24px">Server settings</h2></div>
    <div class="card-flat">
      <table>
        <tr><th>SETTING</th><th style="text-align:right">VALUE</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Version</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">{SERVER.loader} {SERVER.mcVersion}</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Gamemode</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">{SERVER.gamemode}</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>View distance</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">{SERVER.viewDistance}</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Max players</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">{SERVER.maxPlayers}</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Whitelist</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">on</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Online mode</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">on</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>World border</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">none</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Backups</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">nightly 04:00, off-site</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Distant Horizons</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">3.2.0-b server-side</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>World</td><td style="text-align:right"><span class="val">pregenerated</span></td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
